					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zachary-maxwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2975899); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2975899&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606056659" alt="Zachary Maxwell" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2975899)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zachary-maxwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2975899); return false;" >Zachary Maxwell</a></span> <span class="odate time_1513531269 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Dec 2017 17:21</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3654087">
									

<p>You'll understand why this has so many chapters when I get to the Too Real conclusion.</p>
<p>I know I'm skipping over some parts of baby care (for example, sterilising bottles, using baby wipes and powder when changing nappies, etc.) but just assume that this stuff doesn't matter/is done without narration in-universe.</p>
<p>The entity involved has the mind of a child, so doesn't really think of the more complicated, adult-based needs of an infant, but knows about hunger and entertainment at least.</p>

							</div>

								
					
